&lt;li&gt;You own and maintain the security and technology risk framework across infrastructure, applications, cloud, trading systems, and third-party services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You advise management and risk committees using clear reporting on risk indicators, incidents, vulnerabilities, and remediation progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You lead compliance with MAS technology risk requirements by translating regulations into controls, monitoring, testing, and audit-ready evidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You oversee related cyber incident response processes, including detection, containment, recovery, and post-incident analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You evaluate third-party and outsourcing risk, including vendor controls, contractual obligations, and ongoing risk monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support after hours emergency incidents as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 8+ years of experience in information security, cyber risk, or technology risk within financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience working in a MAS-regulated financial institution such as a brokerage, bank, payments firm, or wealth platform&lt;/li&gt;
